@startuml arquitectura-linkguard
title Arquitectura LinkGuard: Componentes y Flujos

package "Orchestrator Host" {
    [Orchestrator\n(:8000/RPC2)] as Orch
    [Hub Agent\n(:9000/RPC2)] as Hub
    database "state.json" as State
    database "events.jsonl" as Events
    file "/etc/linkguard/secrets" as Secrets
    file "/etc/linkguard/jwt_secret" as JWT
}

package "Peer Host(s)" {
    [wg-auto-register\n(peer_register)] as Peer
    file "wg0.conf" as WGConf
    file "wg-auto.json" as PeerState
    file "/etc/linkguard/peer.env" as PeerEnv
}

package "Red WireGuard" {
    cloud "wg-HUB\n(Hub Agent)" as WGHUB
    cloud "wg0\n(Peer)" as WG0
}

Orch --> State : lee/escribe
Orch --> Events : append
Orch --> Secrets : ADMIN_TOKEN\nORCH_TOKEN\nHUB_AGENT_TOKEN
Orch --> JWT : JWT signing key

Orch <--> Hub : XML-RPC\nHUB_AGENT_TOKEN
Hub --> WGHUB : wg set / wg-quick

Peer --> PeerEnv : carga vars
Peer --> PeerState : lee/escribe JWT\nconfig_version
Peer --> WGConf : genera .conf
Peer --> WG0 : wg syncconf

Peer <--> Orch : XML-RPC\nauth.login/refresh\npeer.register/heartbeat\nconfig.get_peer_config

Peer ..> Hub : (indirecto via Orch)

note right of Orch
  **Responsabilidades**:
  - Gestión de usuarios/tenants
  - Asignación de IPs por red
  - Control de quotas (global)
  - Distribución de configs
  - Auto-approve de peers
  - Backup automático
end note

note left of Peer
  **Responsabilidades**:
  - Generar claves WireGuard
  - Registrarse con orchestrator
  - Heartbeat cada 25s
  - Detectar NAT type
  - Aplicar configs dinámicamente
  - Probar reachability (hub-mesh)
end note

note bottom of Hub
  **Responsabilidades**:
  - Gestionar wg-HUB interface
  - Aplicar AllowedIPs por peer
  - NAT/masquerade (iptables)
  - sysctl forwarding
end note

@enduml
